      "date": "2026-11-07 15:13:27.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(6 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. In both new paths, pages that belong to an object being replaced can end up written back to the unavailable OST, and the discard then waits for that write. That is the situation the series is trying to avoid. This also fixes the still-unlanded parent change 66882 in the same series, so it might be simpler to fold it in there. Either way, a sanity test that dirties pages on a stripe of an inactive OST and then does truncate(0) would help, for example with a PFL component start that is not chunk aligned, and with a concurrent mmap write.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    },
