      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "f0d391db9bf9ca39481477acf2acc4007c62a704",
            "subject": "LU-20211 mdt: trunc(0) layout replace on inactive stripes"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-05 19:53:03.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-05 20:24:16.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20211 osc: discard a truncate size range from cache",
        "message": "LU-20211 osc: discard a truncate size range from cache\n\nTo replace the objects of an unavailable OST past a truncate size,\nthe client discards its dirty pages from the page after the size\nbefore the layout change, since the replaced objects hold no data\nbefore the size.  That discard is page aligned, but\nosc_cache_writeback_range() drops whole extents and asserts that the\nchunk-aligned range contains each extent, which is only true for a\nlock cancel.  An extent that starts before the range would hit the\nassertion, or with 1MiB ZFS chunks lose the dirty pages below the\nsize.  Write such an extent back instead: only a kept object maps\ndata below the size, and the truncate punch removes the rest.\n\nAn active extent of an mmap write racing the discard asserted too.\nLeave it to the truncate instead.  mdc_io_fsync_start() discarded\nthe whole DoM object for any range: discard only the requested range.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia32e8e3e17a29843aeb71a243afd4b86063ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
